1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,043
Last time you played somebody else's universe.

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:06,537
This is the first minute of yours.

3
00:00:06,987 --> 00:00:18,291
A title, a place to start with a name you gave it, and a save file, so the game you stop tonight is still there tomorrow.

4
00:00:18,741 --> 00:00:23,959
One file of your own, and a few words changed in another.

5
00:00:25,159 --> 00:00:27,767
ou is the Open Universe template.

6
00:00:28,217 --> 00:00:31,261
The title goes in the mission list.

7
00:00:31,711 --> 00:00:34,754
Keep it to letters, numbers and spaces.

8
00:00:35,204 --> 00:00:37,813
No hyphen, no colon, no apostrophe.

9
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:49,567
That is not fussiness: the title is copied into a small settings file, and a hyphen in that file stops the whole game from starting. Lint.

10
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:53,930
Clean, and I have not written a word yet.

11
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:56,870
Three files matter today.

12
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:06,450
The universe itself, which I write. story.mast, which tells the game which universe file to load and what to call it.

13
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:09,943
And description.yaml, which already has my title.

14
00:01:10,393 --> 00:01:12,133
The rest is machinery.

15
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:16,376
My file, my name: small letters, underscores.

16
00:01:16,826 --> 00:01:19,870
Inside, one record with a single hash.

17
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:22,493
That is the universe itself.

18
00:01:22,943 --> 00:01:30,770
The name in square brackets, a key in round ones, and under the fence, what this place is.

19
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:36,437
I am writing this for me and for whoever writes with me.

20
00:01:36,887 --> 00:01:39,061
Players never see this record.

21
00:01:39,511 --> 00:01:42,989
It is the title page of the manuscript.

22
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:46,483
What players read comes in a minute.

23
00:01:47,683 --> 00:01:49,422
Two hashes: a chapter.

24
00:01:49,872 --> 00:01:56,393
Its key has to be scenario, because that is the word the game looks for.

25
00:01:56,843 --> 00:01:58,583
And one fact: Mode.

26
00:01:59,033 --> 00:02:02,076
Story is one ship and an ending.

27
00:02:02,526 --> 00:02:05,570
Campaign is one ship over many nights.

28
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,193
Sandbox is an open world.

29
00:02:08,643 --> 00:02:10,817
Today those three play alike.

30
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:16,920
The word starts to matter when we add fleets, late in this class.

31
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:19,978
Write the one that is true.

32
00:02:21,178 --> 00:02:24,222
Sides and Jobs came with the template.

33
00:02:24,672 --> 00:02:27,715
I leave them for the next lectures.

34
00:02:28,165 --> 00:02:32,078
At the end, a new chapter: Landmarks. One place.

35
00:02:32,528 --> 00:02:37,746
At: 0, 0 is home, where every new game starts. Kind: station.

36
00:02:38,196 --> 00:02:40,804
And one line under the fence.

37
00:02:41,254 --> 00:02:53,428
That line is the first thing my crew reads when they arrive, so it stays on one line: the card shows the first line and nothing after it.

38
00:02:54,628 --> 00:02:55,628
Four changes.

39
00:02:56,078 --> 00:02:59,122
The title: search, four found, replace all.

40
00:02:59,572 --> 00:03:02,615
The file name: two found, replace all.

41
00:03:03,065 --> 00:03:07,848
If those numbers are not four and two, stop and look.

42
00:03:08,298 --> 00:03:12,646
Third, the two lines that start with a double quote.

43
00:03:13,096 --> 00:03:19,617
These are what players read on the start screen, so these are worth writing well.

44
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:22,241
No curly brackets in them.

45
00:03:22,691 --> 00:03:25,735
And fourth, two lines I leave alone.

46
00:03:26,185 --> 00:03:29,228
The first gives Helm an Engage button.

47
00:03:29,678 --> 00:03:35,330
The second keeps a list of the named places the crew has been.

48
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:40,563
Without them, your universe is one system with no way out.

49
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:43,067
Two commands now.

50
00:03:43,517 --> 00:03:45,691
Lint reads my universe file.

51
00:03:46,141 --> 00:03:51,793
Compile reads story.mast, and when it is happy it says nothing at all.

52
00:03:52,243 --> 00:03:54,417
Watch what each one catches.

53
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:57,476
A misspelled mode: lint tells me.

54
00:03:57,926 --> 00:04:06,622
One hash too few on Scenario: lint says clean, and in the game every chapter below it would be gone.

55
00:04:07,072 --> 00:04:17,072
And a single letter different in the title here: both commands are happy, and the game would start with no universe in it.

56
00:04:17,522 --> 00:04:24,043
So I count hashes by eye, one, two, three, and I never retype the title.

57
00:04:24,493 --> 00:04:26,667
I search and replace it.

58
00:04:27,867 --> 00:04:28,867
My title.

59
00:04:29,317 --> 00:04:30,622
My two lines.

60
00:04:31,072 --> 00:04:38,028
Start is on Continue, and there is nothing to continue, so this is a new game.

61
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:42,826
And there is the card: Kestrel Relay, and my line.

62
00:04:43,276 --> 00:04:45,450
Comms takes a cargo run.

63
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,204
Helm engages it.

64
00:04:47,654 --> 00:04:49,393
We are somewhere else.

65
00:04:49,843 --> 00:04:55,496
And in the quest list, a charted location: Kestrel Relay, the way home.

66
00:04:55,946 --> 00:04:58,989
Now I stop, here, away from home.

67
00:04:59,439 --> 00:05:01,178
This is the save.

68
00:05:01,628 --> 00:05:08,150
It is named after my title, and it knows where I stopped. Start again. Continue.

69
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,339
Same system, same money.

70
00:05:10,789 --> 00:05:13,398
Engage the way home. Kestrel Relay.

71
00:05:13,848 --> 00:05:16,022
Two warnings about that file.

72
00:05:16,472 --> 00:05:22,993
Its name comes from the title, so a new title is a new, empty game.

73
00:05:23,443 --> 00:05:28,226
And New Game on the start screen replaces it without asking.

74
00:05:29,426 --> 00:05:31,165
Now make it yours.

75
00:05:31,615 --> 00:05:35,963
Your title, your file, your two lines, your front door.

76
00:05:36,413 --> 00:05:43,804
Then break it once on purpose, one letter, and learn where the game tells you about it.

77
00:05:44,254 --> 00:05:52,515
Next time we throw out the two factions that came in the box and write three of your own.
